WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.400
The template classes, as a checklist.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.674
ESC1: a template lets the requester supply
the subject or subject alternative name,

3
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:12.413
permits client authentication, and
broad unprivileged groups can enroll,

4
00:00:12.413 --> 00:00:16.388
so a member could obtain a
certificate that names someone else.

5
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:19.630
Detect it with Defender
for Identity, and by hand:

6
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.631
Supply in the request on
the Subject Name tab,

7
00:00:22.631 --> 00:00:27.739
an authentication purpose such as Client
Authentication, Smart Card Logon,

8
00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:32.118
PKINIT or Any Purpose, and Enroll
granted to Authenticated Users,

9
00:00:32.118 --> 00:00:35.037
Domain Users, Domain
Computers or Everyone.

10
00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:39.324
On the CA, events 4886
and 4887 show requests

11
00:00:39.324 --> 00:00:44.325
where the requester and
the issued subject differ.

12
00:00:44.325 --> 00:00:49.098
Any one remediation closes it: build
the subject from Active Directory,

13
00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:54.436
remove authentication EKUs the template
doesn't need, restrict Enroll, require

14
00:00:54.436 --> 00:00:59.775
CA certificate manager approval, or take
the template off every CA if it's unused.

15
00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:05.125
ESC2 is Any Purpose or no EKU on
a broadly enrollable template.

16
00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:08.649
A no-EKU template restricted
to PKI administrators,

17
00:01:08.649 --> 00:01:12.500
such as a subordinate CA
template, isn't the same exposure.

18
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.750
ESC3 is a broadly enrollable
enrollment agent template.

19
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.062
Treat an enrollment agent certificate
as an impersonation capability.

20
00:01:21.062 --> 00:01:25.856
Microsoft doesn't publish a Windows
Server 2025 procedure for enrollment

21
00:01:25.856 --> 00:01:30.650
agent restrictions, so validate the
existing configuration in a lab first.

22
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.161
ESC4 is write rights or
ownership on a template

23
00:01:34.161 --> 00:01:37.312
held by anyone but the PKI administrators.

24
00:01:37.312 --> 00:01:41.375
Changes are logged as event
5136 only when directory

25
00:01:41.375 --> 00:01:45.900
change auditing is on and the
objects carry a matching SACL.

26
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:51.204
One trap when you fix it: if you remove
Authenticated Users from a template ACL,

27
00:01:51.204 --> 00:01:54.353
grant each issuing CA's
computer account Read,

28
00:01:54.353 --> 00:01:57.140
or the CA can no longer read the template.
